<title>PERU: Peru's October coffee output falls to 94 tonnes.</title>
<headline>Peru's October coffee output falls to 94 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's October coffee production fell to 94 tonnes from 354 tonnes in the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Thursday.</p>
<p>Coffee output for the first ten months rose to 107,143 tonnes from 96,622 tonnes in the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>Non-decaffeinated coffee exports fell 53.7 percent in October to $15.5 million, while exports in the first ten months fell 14.5 percent to $201.6 million, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Peru, whose principal coffee harvest is between April and November, is South America's number four producer after Brazil, Colombia and Ecuador, according to the government.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
